5. Advertising

Sadaf VPN is a free, advertisement-supported VPN application. Advertisements are provided through Google AdMob and help support the operation and maintenance of the service.

Google AdMob may use your advertising ID, device information, approximate location, and other permitted information to display personalized or contextual advertisements and measure advertising performance.

You can manage or delete your advertising ID and adjust advertising privacy preferences through your Android device settings, usually under Settings > Google > All services > Ads or Settings > Privacy > Ads, depending on your device and Android version.

Where required by applicable law, we or our advertising partners request consent before using personal information for personalized advertising.

Advertising preferences may affect the types of advertisements displayed but do not necessarily remove advertisements from the app.

6. Data Sharing and International Transfers

We do not sell your personal information.

We share information only in the following circumstances:

- With the third-party service providers listed in section 4, to support advertising, analytics, crash reporting, notifications, and other app functionality.
- When required by applicable law, legal process, or governmental authority.
- When reasonably necessary to protect the rights, safety, and security of our users, our service, and others.

Our servers and those of our service providers may be located in different countries. Your information may therefore be processed or stored outside your country of residence.

Where applicable law requires safeguards for international data transfers, we take appropriate measures to protect the transferred information.

7. Data Retention

We retain information only as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy, subject to applicable legal obligations.

- Installation, device, and activity records: Retained while the app is in use and for as long as reasonably necessary for service operation, security, diagnostics, and other stated purposes.
- IP address history: Limited to the most recent 100 entries per installation. Older entries are removed automatically.
- Crash reports, analytics, and advertising data: Retained by the respective third-party service providers according to their own data retention policies.
- Support communications: Retained for as long as reasonably necessary to respond to requests and maintain support records.

8. Your Choices and Rights

You have several options to control your information:

- Uninstalling the app: You can uninstall Sadaf VPN at any time. This removes app data stored locally on your device, subject to Android's data management behavior. Uninstalling does not automatically delete information already stored on our servers.
- Access and deletion requests: You may request access to or deletion of the information we hold about your installation by contacting us using the email address provided below.
- Advertising preferences: You may manage your advertising ID and advertising personalization preferences through your device settings and any consent options provided by the app.
- Notifications: You can allow or disable notifications through your device's app settings.

Depending on your location, you may have additional privacy rights under applicable laws, including the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) or the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA).

To exercise your applicable privacy rights, contact us at sadaf.support.vpn@gmail.com.

9. Data Security

We use reasonable technical and organizational safeguards designed to protect information against unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure.

Communication between the app and our servers is encrypted, and access to our databases is restricted to authorized systems and personnel.

However, no method of internet transmission or electronic data storage is completely secure. We cannot guarantee absolute security.

